<p>I agree wholeheartedly with the opinion on this not being a good AWCY? article. It's a neat skip, but doesn't use the GOI association in a way I particularly enjoy for pretty much all reasons stated.</p>
<p>As I a reader, however, I'll be brief and say the commentary on the characterization of Gloria and Bellamy feels unwarranted. While the story, unfortunately, does depicts an incredibly distasteful situation on the subject of race, it seems purely incidental - not only does it seem like the author had no interest going in such a direction but, also, the article is written in such a way people are supposed to sympathize with 3126 which, stuck into a shitty relationship, was a victim of a massive AWCY?-obsessed jerk.</p>
<p>This is a story about how a good person was tricked by her selfish lover. Reading this much between the lines, in my opinion, could lead people to actually AVOID being more diverse when writing. TL;DR:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I can not conceive of anyone who isn't white being okay with selling someone into slavery</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This line pretty much sums it up in terms of what I disagree with. Everybody can be an asshole.</p>

