<p>I will say to avoid circles ad infinitum (and also because I have appointments to get to today &lt;.&lt;):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I am merely concerned that, by citing this as a reason to downvote the article, other authors would simply avoid the subject entirely instead of bothering with the possibility of being intensive.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd concede that there's perhaps a small chance that this would happen were it to be my sole reason. I made sure to specify it's not. Specific racism WRT this subject is not something I'm qualified to speak on personally (as I'm mixed Brazilian), but I think there's a good amount of people who would genuinely appreciate someone trying earnestly and in good faith while fucking up than someone who just doesn't care to try.</p>
<p>And again; I don't think the author did this intentionally, nor are they to really blame. I think it's easy to write something like this and overlook what the implications of the writing might be. And my intention here isn't to shame the author here; merely point out what I see and interpret and read, so that hopefully people understand where I'm coming from and how to improve on such things in the future. I take critique seriously; it's one of my passions whenever I do it.</p>

