<blockquote>
<p>There seems to be this fairly recent trend of characterizing AWCY? as evil art bastards that do evil things for art</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This isn't a new trend, though. AWCY has <em>always</em> been a group of art-terrorists doing terrible things that they pretentiously and ignorantly call art.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And the reason why I suspect all these characters who are not our skip are white is because that is the typical &quot;default&quot; for characters when their ethnicity and race is not specified, and I can not conceive of anyone who isn't white being okay with selling someone into slavery</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I find this statement concerning on several levels. Firstly, it assumes that &quot;white people&quot; exist as a category<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-217545-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-217545-1')">1</a></sup> and that they are subhumans who are inherently okay with slavery. I'll also point out that I cannot find a place where it specifies the girlfriend's race. You are assuming she is white because being white makes her capable of being a bad person, and that a non-white person would be incapable of the same act. There is a word for this. Several, actually.</p>
<p>Secondly, it ignores the massive global problem of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_trafficking">human trafficking</a> and the disturbing fetishization of pimping in numerous subcultures, and the concept of toxic relationships- all of which are problems that surpass melanin production rates and bone structure.</p>
